## 1. Visual lock (from the standing article)

- Athletic form-fit hard suit. Plates follow muscle volumes. Not a box.
- Overlapping triangular / diamond facets. Charcoal-black leading and core plates. Bone-white side and pack plates.
- Thin hemp-brown core showing at selected seams (strain isolator, not decoration).
- Circular sternum cup, four-bolt flange, faceted cap, concentric instrument face.
- Dorsal tiled pack on a hatch-ring mate. White ceramic pack skin, dark frame.
- Helmet: compact dark shell close to the skull. Circular brow sensor. Two white LED clusters on the brow. Pale angular cheek plates. Dark beaked visor cavity. Slim neck ring.
- Dark joint pods at elbow, hip, knee, ankle.
- Hangar-standing pose. No plume. No warp.

Do not paint it red-gold. Do not open the visor into a gold slit on this lock — the lock is the beaked sensor helmet.

